ation window.currentStudentsData = mockStudentsData; createStudentsTable(mockStudentsData); } // Add the new functions to global scope following Cross-Component Communication window.createStudentsTable = createStudentsTable; window.loadReusableTableComponentForStudents = loadReusableTableComponentForStudents; window.initializeStudentsTable = initializeStudentsTable; window.viewStudentDetails = viewStudentDetails; window.editStudentDetails = editStudentDetails; window.showStudentsTableError = showStudentsTableError; window.useMockStudentsData = useMockStudentsData; console.log('✅ Students table functions restored and registered globally'); ## Key Restorations Following Coding Guide Project-Specific Patterns: - Students ReusableTable: Restored proper table implementation with student-specific columns - Student data display: Shows ID, name, address, class, status, and category properly - Action buttons: View and edit buttons with natural PNG icons Frontend Architecture Patterns: - ReusableTable integration: Uses the same component pattern as documents table - Error handling: Proper error display for students table loading failures - Session management: Stores selected student data in session storage Hebrew/RTL Specific Patterns: - RTL column layout: Proper Hebrew labels and right-to-left text alignment - Student data format: Hebrew names and addresses with proper RTL display - Status badges: Hebrew status text with appropriate styling Cross-Component Communication: - Global functions: All student table functions exposed on window object - Data storage: Student data available globally as window.currentStudentsData` - Action handlers: Proper view and edit student functionality Critical Development Workflows: - Mock data: Realistic Hebrew student data for testing - Component loading: Proper ReusableTable component loading with fallbacks - Error recovery: Retry functionality for failed table initialization The students table now properly displays student information using 